==Battleground==
*3 [[Wild Doge]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 33.33~36.67 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,100f</sup>.
*5 [[Brollow]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.
*1 [[Suidae Piggicus]] spawns after 23.33 seconds<sup>700f</sup>.
*1 [[Raynard]] spawns after 23.33 seconds<sup>700f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Pterowl Hazuku]] spawns as the boss.
**1 [[Suidae Piggicus]] spawns.
**Infinite [[Squire Rel]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 8~11.33 seconds<sup>240f~340f</sup>.
**1 [[Great Angel Chibinel]] spawns after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.
**3 [[Imperator Sael]]s spawn after 80 seconds<sup>2,400f</sup>, delay 60~63.33 seconds<sup>1,800f~1,900f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Wild Doge]]s spawn after 80 seconds<sup>2,400f</sup>, delay 60~63.33 seconds<sup>1,800f~1,900f</sup>.
**6 [[Brollow]]s spawn after 80 seconds<sup>2,400f</sup>, delay 26.67~30 seconds<sup>800f~900f</sup>.

==Strategy==
While a majority of the threats here are Long-Distance and cannot hit up close, they make hitting Imperator Saels much harder, with the occasional Wild Doge or Brollow not helping at all. With Pterowl Hazuku doing massive damage and potentially throwing a Surge into your defenses and Great Angel Chibinel frequently Slowing and Weakening the cats that get close, this stage is ''very'' hard if not tackled properly. As such, the easiest way to clear this stage is to defeat the base before an Imperator Sael gets the chance to spawn.

The start of the level can be annoying to stall for cash in, as there's a chance that [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] can run in and kill Raynard once it's dealt with the last of the peons that spawn at the start. While it's safe to use Courier to kill Suidae Piggicus since he will eventually die to Wild Doge and Brollow, avoid using it after this point so you can allow your Erasers to enter the lone Raynard's blindspot. Raynard DOES have very low HP, to the point that many Erasers can knock him back over time; try to get Raynard halfway to your base so you can kill him before he gets knocked behind the enemy base. Spawn [[Elder Beast Naala (Special Cat)|Awakened Naala]] so it can start damaging the frontlines and ravaging the base as soon as the boss wave starts.

Fortunately, Suidae Piggicus has a weak offense, so it will go down quickly. Fast units like [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]], [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]], and [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] who can get in Pterowl's blindspot and deal good damage help significantly. [[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Doron]] is useful for reaching and damaging Chibinel when he spawns. [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone Cat]] temporarily stops Wild Doge and Brollow from wreaking havoc. [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] is a given. Do try to prioritize using Long-Distance units like Courier and Housewife, however. Fishman and Awakened Bahamut, for example, cannot easily hit the base with Pterowl present.

Before Suidae Piggicus has a chance to move forward on the boss wave, [[Cat Cannon|the Thunderbolt cannon]] can help by freezing Hazuku to more safely get units into his blindspot.

You can actually cheese the stage with the Thunderbolt cannon by simply freezing the enemies on base hit, then getting units into Hazuku's blindspot. This strategy requires a very high level Thunderbolt, level 20 or possibly even higher, but allows you to destroy the base without letting Pterowl Hazuku move, possibly without even killing him at all.

